## API Rule Summary

### Current Rules

| Collection | List | View | Create | Update | Delete |
|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|:---|
| tenants | Auth | Auth | Commander | Commander | Commander |
| projects | Auth | Auth | Cmd/Op | Cmd/Op | Commander |
| api_keys | Auth | Auth | Cmd/Op | Cmd/Op | Commander |
| roles | Auth | Auth | Commander | Commander | Commander |
| memberships | Auth | Auth | Commander | Commander | Commander |
| model_policies | Auth | Auth | Cmd/Op | Cmd/Op | Commander |
| quotas | Auth | Auth | Commander | Commander | Commander |
| idempotency_records | Service-only | Service-only | Service-only | Service-only | Service-only |
| audit_events | Auth (tenant-scoped) | Auth (tenant-scoped) | Service-only | None | Commander |

**Legend:**
- Auth = `@request.auth.id != ''`
- Commander = `@request.auth.role = 'commander'`
- Cmd/Op = `@request.auth.role = 'commander' || @request.auth.role = 'operator'`
- Service-only = restricted to service account auth/rules
- Public = `null` (no restrictions, avoid for control-plane writes)

### Tenant-Scoped Access Pattern

To implement tenant-scoped access (users can only see their tenant's data):

```javascript
// Example for projects collection
listRule: "@request.auth.id != '' && tenant_id = @request.auth.tenant_id"
viewRule: "@request.auth.id != '' && tenant_id = @request.auth.tenant_id"
```

