## Retention Policy Implementation

### 90-Day Retention for audit_events and idempotency_records

#### Option 1: PocketBase Cron Job (Recommended)

Create a scheduled cleanup script:

```javascript
// pb_hooks/cleanup.pb.js
onRecordBeforeCreateRequest((e) => {
  // Run cleanup every hour
  if (e.collection.name === "audit_events") {
    const dao = new Dao(e.httpContext);
    const cutoffDate = new Date();
    cutoffDate.setDate(cutoffDate.getDate() - 90);
    
    // Delete old audit events
    dao.db()
      .newQuery("DELETE FROM audit_events WHERE timestamp < {:cutoff}")
      .bind({ cutoff: cutoffDate.toISOString() })
      .execute();
  }
});
```

#### Option 2: External Cron Job

```bash
#!/bin/bash
# cleanup-old-records.sh

# Calculate cutoff date (90 days ago)
CUTOFF_DATE=$(date -d "90 days ago" -u +"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")

# Authenticate as admin
TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST https://pocketbase.thynaptic.com/api/admins/auth-with-password \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"identity":"admin@email.com","password":"ADMIN_PASSWORD"}' | jq -r '.token')

# Delete old audit events
curl -X DELETE "https://pocketbase.thynaptic.com/api/collections/audit_events/records" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d "filter=timestamp<'$CUTOFF_DATE'"

# Delete old idempotency records
curl -X DELETE "https://pocketbase.thynaptic.com/api/collections/idempotency_records/records" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d "filter=expires_at<'$CUTOFF_DATE'"

echo "✅ Cleanup completed"
```

Add to crontab:
```bash
# Run daily at 2 AM
0 2 * * * /path/to/cleanup-old-records.sh
```

#### Option 3: Direct Database Cleanup

```sql
-- Delete audit events older than 90 days
DELETE FROM audit_events 
WHERE timestamp < datetime('now', '-90 days');

-- Delete expired idempotency records
DELETE FROM idempotency_records 
WHERE expires_at < datetime('now');

-- Vacuum to reclaim space
VACUUM;
```

Schedule via cron:
```bash
# Daily cleanup at 2 AM
0 2 * * * sqlite3 /pb_data/data.db < /path/to/cleanup.sql
```

